DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-11T07:19:59.1677495Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=187132718800 load_duration=46173000 prompt_eval_count=173 prompt_eval_duration=7572000000 eval_count=769 eval_duration=179513000000 response='Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the requirement to sign in:\n\n### Module: Sign In\n- **Test Scenario**: Successful Sign-In with Valid Credentials\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-SIGNIN-001 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user has a valid account with the system.\n    - The user\'s credentials are correct and up-to-date.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Navigate to the sign-in page.\n    2. Enter the username and password correctly.\n    3. Click the "Sign In" button.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system redirects the user to their dashboard or desired landing page.\n    - The user\'s session is established, and they can access restricted areas.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Valid username and password combination.\n    - Invalid username and valid password combination.\n    - Valid username and invalid password combination.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs the successful sign-in attempt.\n    - Check that the system enforces password policies (e.g., length, complexity).\n\n### Module: Sign In\n- **Test Scenario**: Unsuccessful Sign-In with Invalid Credentials\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-SIGNIN-002 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user does not have a valid account with the system.\n    - The user\'s credentials are incorrect or outdated.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Navigate to the sign-in page.\n    2. Enter invalid username and password combination.\n    3. Click the "Sign In" button.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system displays an error message indicating invalid credentials.\n    - The user is not redirected to their dashboard or restricted areas.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Invalid username and password combination.\n    - Username only (password omitted).\n    - Password only (username omitted).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs the failed sign-in attempt.\n    - Check that the system enforces rate limiting to prevent brute-force attacks.\n\n### Module: Sign In\n- **Test Scenario**: Forgotten Password Recovery\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-SIGNIN-003 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user has a valid account with the system.\n    - The user\'s password is forgotten or needs to be reset.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Navigate to the sign-in page.\n    2. Click the "Forgot Password" link.\n    3. Enter the username associated with the forgotten password.\n    4. Follow the system\'s instructions for resetting the password.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system sends a password reset email or displays a temporary password.\n    - The user can reset their password and gain access to their account.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Valid username and correct email address.\n    - Invalid username and correct email address.\n    - Correct username and invalid email address.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs the password reset request.\n    - Check that the system enforces password policies (e.g., length, complexity) for new passwords.\n\nThese test scenarios cover various sign-in scenarios, including successful and unsuccessful attempts, as well as forgotten password recovery. They also highlight security implications, edge cases, and compliance checks to ensure comprehensive testing of the sign-in feature.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262